.vscode/

# User data (don't commit personal settings or content)
settings.json
logs/
**/.claude/settings.local.json
# Shared Claude Code project settings ARE tracked: worktree.baseRef must travel
# between machines or lanes silently branch from main instead of the port branch.
# This negation must stay below the bare `settings.json` rule above to win.
!.claude/settings.json

# Claude Code port orchestration run state (.port/): WAVE-LOCK, LOOP-LOCK, STOP,
# handoff.md and phase/audit logs. This is per-machine execution state, never shared.
# It MUST be ignored: the phase prompt writes .port/WAVE-LOCK while a wave runs, and an
# unignored .port/ leaves `git status` dirty, which makes the fail-closed blind audit
# report a false FAIL on a perfectly good tree — the exact class that halted a run under
# the old engine. The durable queue is client/docs/task-board.md, not this directory.
.port/

# Pi port orchestration
# Share the exact project package declaration, but not installed npm contents or
# crash-safe task run state. Pi restores the pinned package after project trust.
!.pi/settings.json
.pi/npm/
.pi-tasks/

