# Build & Release Artifacts
release/
publish/
# ...except the port's publish HARNESS, which is source, not output.
#
# SAME DEFECT AS THE `tools/` RULE BELOW, found 2026-08-18 and fixed the same way.
# Bare `publish/` matches at ANY depth, so it silently swallows `client/tools/publish/`.
# Its four scripts survive only because they predate the rule — exactly the escape the
# `tools/` comment describes — but every NEW file added there was being ignored, and a
# lane that added a publish script would have watched it vanish with a clean build and
# no error. `git check-ignore` hides this for tracked paths; `--no-index` shows it.
# The negation is on the DIRECTORY because git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded.
!client/tools/publish/
bin/
obj/
.vs/
*.user
crash_log.txt

